.TH tkutlfind n 0.3 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutlfind
.PP
Incremental find with match highlighting for a \fBtablelist\fR widget. Unlike a filter (which hides non\-matching rows), \fBtkutlfind\fR highlights the matching cells and lets you step through them with next/prev. Complements \fBtkutils::tkufilterbar\fR. Library\-neutral.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutlfind 0.3
.CE
.PP
Requires \fBTk\fR and \fBtablelist\fR.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlfind::find    tbl query ?options?   ;# -> match count, highlights
::tkutils::tkutlfind::next    tbl                   ;# -> {row col} | {}
::tkutils::tkutlfind::prev    tbl                   ;# -> {row col} | {}
::tkutils::tkutlfind::matches tbl                   ;# -> list of {row col}
::tkutils::tkutlfind::clear   tbl
.CE
.PP
\fBnext\fR/\fBprev\fR cycle through the matches (wrapping), scrolling each into view (\fBseecell\fR) and activating its row.
.SS "Options (find)"
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-columns\fR	all visible	columns to search
\fB\-mode\fR	\fBsubstring\fR	\fBsubstring\fR, \fBexact\fR, \fBglob\fR, \fBregexp\fR
\fB\-nocase\fR	\fB1\fR	case\-insensitive matching
\fB\-highlightbg\fR	\fB#ffe9a8\fR	background for matching cells
\fB\-highlightfg\fR	\fB{}\fR	optional foreground for matching cells
\fB\-hidden\fR	\fB0\fR	also search hidden rows
.TE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require Tk
package require tablelist_tile
package require tkutils::tkutlfind

# search box that highlights as you type
entry .e -textvariable q
bind .e <KeyRelease> { ::tkutils::tkutlfind::find .t $q }
bind .e <Return>     { ::tkutils::tkutlfind::next .t }

# F3 / Shift-F3 to step through matches
bind . <F3>       { ::tkutils::tkutlfind::next .t }
bind . <Shift-F3> { ::tkutils::tkutlfind::prev .t }
.CE
.PP
Search only one column with a regular expression:
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlfind::find .t {^A.*t$} -mode regexp -columns 0
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Matching uses the \fBdisplayed\fR values (\fBgetformatted\fR), so it finds what the user sees (e.g. formatted numbers from \fBtkutlfmt\fR).
.IP \(bu
Matches are kept as row keys: after the user sorts, \fBmatches\fR, \fBnext\fR and \fBprev\fR give the current row indices. Rows deleted since \fBfind\fR are skipped. Re\-run \fBfind\fR after the cell contents change.
.IP \(bu
Hidden rows (for example from \fBtkutlfilter\fR) are skipped unless \fB\-hidden 1\fR. A match inside a collapsed tree node is revealed (its ancestors expanded) when \fBnext\fR/\fBprev\fR reaches it.
.IP \(bu
\fBclear\fR restores the cell colours that were set before \fBfind\fR.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLFIND <REASON>}\fR (\fBMODE\fR, \fBOPTION\fR).
